# Line endings
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which would write CRLF into the working
# tree on a fresh clone while the repository stores LF. That mismatch is what
# produces the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings, and it makes formatters
# and linters disagree with git about what changed.
#
# Declaring it here settles it for every clone on every OS, regardless of each
# developer's local git config: text files are LF in the repository and LF on
# disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.hbc binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Marking them keeps them out of language statistics
# and collapses them in diffs, where reading them line by line helps nobody.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
